// A global shared between an ISR (via the inc_count helper) and main must be
// volatile, and the ISR must not read-modify-write it (that is non-atomic). This
// is enforced TRANSITIVELY through the helper call (ISR-TRANS fix) — pre-fix the
// non-volatile form compiled silently and hoisted/torn on real hardware.
//
// BUG-792: this helper used to be `irq_count = irq_count + 1`, which is exactly
// the read-modify-write the comment above forbids — it only compiled because the
// rule tested for a compound OPERATOR (`+=`) rather than for the OPERATION, so
// writing the RMW out in full evaded it. The rule now catches both spellings, so
// the fixture is a plain volatile STORE: still an ISR->helper->global access
// (which is what this test exercises), no longer a torn RMW.
volatile u32 irq_count = 0;
void inc_count() { irq_count = 1; }
interrupt USART1 {
    inc_count();
}
